What is 2,5-Dihydroxy-1,4-Dithiane (DHDT)?
2,5-Dihydroxy‑1,4‑dithiane is a white‑to‑beige sulfur‑containing heterocyclic solid, commonly described as the dimer of mercaptoacetaldehyde. Its unique bis‑hydroxyl structure makes it a versatile building block for synthesising sulfur‑rich pharmaceuticals such as lamivudine and emtricitabine, while its pleasant savory aroma finds applications as a flavoring agent in food and beverage formulations.
